All Rights Reserved
===================

Copyright (c) 2026 caohaotiantian <caohaotiantian@gmail.com>

This is **not** an open-source licence, and it grants nothing new. It writes down the position
that already applied: the repository is private and carried no LICENSE file, and the default for
a work with no licence is exclusive copyright. Anyone with access was therefore holding code
they had no stated right to run, derive cases from, or publish a replayed number from — which is
a worse position than this notice, not a better one, because it was undefined rather than
restrictive.

Grant
-----

No permission to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell copies of
this software is granted except by written agreement with the copyright holder.

People given access to this repository by the copyright holder may run it internally for
evaluation and development. That permission does not extend to redistribution, to publishing
results derived from it, or to the case sets and run artifacts — see below.

Data
----

The case sets, drafts, run directories and archives are **not** covered by any grant here at
all, and are excluded from the repository on purpose. They contain verbatim source from real
projects (measured 0%–91.2% of a reverse-constructed case's substantive lines), personal account
names, and unsanitised filesystem paths. `docs/design/2026-07-25-ai-coding-benchmark.md` §
forbids sharing them before desensitisation, and `docs/SESSION-2026-08-14.md` §5.3 records that
desensitisation as incomplete. Ask before requesting any of it.

Contact
-------

Repository, database and gateway access are granted by the copyright holder. See CODEOWNERS.

Changing this
-------------

Replacing this file with an open-source licence is a decision for the copyright holder alone. If
that happens, note that it settles the *code* only: the data above needs its own answer.
